@startuml
' NewEra POS - State diagram of the item status (DR-02), W09
' Team D - editable source of assets/state_item_status.png
' Render with: java -jar plantuml.jar -tpng assets/state_item_status.puml
' Sources: SRS DR-02, FR-33, FR-38, FR-57, BR-11 (review #50, B-D03 and B-D19).

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam dpi 130
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam ArrowColor #444444
skinparam StateBorderColor #1F4E79
skinparam StateBackgroundColor #EAF1FB
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #FFF8DC
skinparam NoteBorderColor #B8A04A
skinparam StateStartColor #444444
skinparam StateEndColor #444444

title NewEra POS - State diagram: status of a rentable item (Item.status)

[*] --> Available : item added to the item list\n(catalog import, IR-17)

Available --> Rented : rental paid and saved\n(UC3 step 15, FR-38)
Rented --> Available : rental return confirmed,\nitem undamaged\n(UC5 step 10, FR-57)
Rented --> UnderMaintenance : rental return confirmed,\ndamage confirmed by a store manager\n(UC5 ext. 6a, FR-52, FR-57)
UnderMaintenance --> Available : a store manager confirms\nthat the item can be rented again\n(DR-02)

state "Under maintenance" as UnderMaintenance

note right of Rented
  A Rented item cannot be rented or sold
  until it is returned (BR-11).
  Open: an item that is never returned
  (lost or stolen) stays Rented and the rental
  stays overdue (BR-12). SRS section 3.5, open point.
end note

note bottom of UnderMaintenance
  Not drawn because no requirement or decision exists yet:
  - the function with which the store manager confirms the repair (no FR yet);
  - retiring an item. An item that is no longer used is marked inactive,
    not deleted (DR-16); this is not an item status.
  The status Reserved was removed in W08 (B-D03).
end note
@enduml
